{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## The problem\n\nThree bot alert lanes close their own alert tickets with an automated `--force=<reason>` —\nthe same gate bypass `AGENTS.md` forbids agents from using and reserves for a human\njudgement call:\n\n- `scripts/dependency_audit.py` `cmd_advisory_alert` (dependency advisories)\n- `scripts/canary_bridge.py` `cmd_heartbeat_alert` (reconcile-bridge heartbeat)\n- `scripts/canary_bridge.py` `cmd_binding_drift_alert` (bridge fsck drift)\n\nEach carries the same stated justification: \"bot alert tickets have no completion\ncriteria to verify\". That justification is accurate — these tickets record an external\ncondition, not a unit of work — but the conclusion drawn from it is wrong. \"This ticket\nclass has nothing to verify\" is an argument for a **disposition path** for such tickets,\nnot for automating the override that exists for human judgement.\n\nRelated to `7147-6ea7-90b4-44b1` (`wooded-timid-gallinule`), which removed the no-verdict force-close path but intentionally left the genuine-clear bot-alert close route for this follow-up.\n\n## Operator-approved design 2026-09-06\n\nUse the existing bounded close-disposition vocabulary rather than an automated `--force` bypass. Bot alert tickets are externally observed conditions; when the detector observes recovery/clear state, the appropriate completion evidence is the detector's own current verdict plus a durable close disposition. The selected route is:\n\n- Close bot alert tickets with `--class env_integration` and no `--force` when the same bot-alert lane that opened/commented the ticket observes the clear condition.\n- Gate the route in core, not by script convention: `env_integration` may bypass completion verification only for tickets carrying bot-alert provenance (`detected_by` / bridge-alert metadata from the alert lane). A normal task/bug without that provenance must still be refused, even if a script tries to use `--class env_integration`.\n- Keep the audit signal stronger than today's absent-attestation force close: the close event records the bounded class and the alert-lane provenance remains on the ticket; no force reason is recorded.\n\nRejected alternatives: a new ticket type or tag adds more mechanism than needed; a wholly new detected-by-scoped close primitive duplicates existing close-class semantics. The approved path reuses close dispositions and narrows the bypass to bot-alert provenance.\n\n## Population to update\n\nThe complete force-close population found for this defect is exactly three bot alert close-on-clear lanes:\n\n1. `scripts/dependency_audit.py::cmd_advisory_alert` closes dependency advisory tickets after zero advisories are observed.\n2. `scripts/canary_bridge.py::cmd_heartbeat_alert` closes reconcile-bridge heartbeat tickets after the bridge is healthy.\n3. `scripts/canary_bridge.py::cmd_binding_drift_alert` closes bridge binding-drift tickets after zero drift findings are observed.\n\nThe implementation must grep the scripts for `--force=` after the change and the targeted tests must fail if any of these three close paths still pass a force flag.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. Add ADR 0117 documenting the operator-approved disposition path and the rejected alternatives.\n2. Add a core close-precheck branch for `--class env_integration` that skips the completion verifier only when the ticket snapshot shows bot-alert provenance from a supported alert lane. Unsupported tickets return a refusal naming the missing bot-alert provenance.\n3. Replace the three script `--force=<reason>` close invocations with the new `--class env_integration` route.\n4. Update the existing 24f7 regression test to assert the advisory-alert close argv survives the real `rebar transition` parser with `--class env_integration` and without `--force`.\n5. Update canary bridge tests for both heartbeat and binding-drift close-on-clear paths to assert `--class env_integration` and no `--force`.\n6. Add a core negative test proving a non-bot-alert ticket using `--class env_integration` is refused, so the route is not a general-purpose bypass.\n\n## Verification plan\n\n- RED first: add/update the script argv tests and the core non-bot negative test before changing implementation.\n- Targeted test command: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py tests/unit/test_bot_alert_disposition.py`.\n- Safety grep: `rg --fixed-strings -- '--force=' scripts/dependency_audit.py scripts/canary_bridge.py` must find no bot-alert close path.\n- Full local gate before Gerrit push: `env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] ADR 0117 records the close-disposition route above and why it is preferred over new ticket type/tag or a new detected-by primitive.\n- [ ] All three bot alert close-on-clear paths (`cmd_advisory_alert`, `cmd_heartbeat_alert`, `cmd_binding_drift_alert`) call `rebar transition ... closed --class env_integration` and never pass `--force`.\n- [ ] All three force-pinning tests move to the new route in the same patch: `tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py::test_advisory_alert_close_argv_survives_the_real_transition_parser`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py::test_heartbeat_alert_closes_on_recovery`, and `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py::test_close_argv_exact_shape`.\n- [ ] A core test proves `--class env_integration` is refused for a non-bot-alert ticket, preserving the close gate for ordinary work.\n- [ ] Targeted tests and the safety grep pass.\n\n\n## Final plan-review amendment 2026-09-07\n\n- Use ADR 0117 (0115 and 0116 already allocated).\n- `env_integration` bypass allowlist is EXACTLY `dependency-advisory-canary`, `heartbeat-canary`, `binding-drift-canary`; no wildcard, and `ci`/`fuzzer`/`human-audit` must fail.\n- Provenance source is ONLY `detected_by`; drop `bridge_alerts` because these scripts emit no BRIDGE_ALERT.\n- Binding-drift coverage is explicit: `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py::test_drift_alert_close_on_recovery` must assert binding-drift close argv contains `--class env_integration` and NO `--force`.\n- Final moved-test inventory: `tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py::test_advisory_alert_close_argv_survives_the_real_transition_parser`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py::test_heartbeat_alert_closes_on_recovery`, `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py::test_close_argv_exact_shape`, and `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge_heldout.py::test_drift_alert_close_on_recovery`; all assert the new disposition path and no `--force` in the same change.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788784735539674001,"uuid":"abba1e36-a22d-4aa2-b89c-37697f7635be"}